                eng: "Today, people use both digital screens and paper every day. Computers and smartphones help us work fast. You can save thousands of files on a phone, and you can send emails anywhere in seconds. Most businesses use digital tools to save time and money.\n\nHowever, paper is still very popular for many tasks. Studies show that most people remember information better when they read from a paper book. Paper does not need electricity, and reading paper does not hurt your eyes like a bright screen.\n\nQuantity words help us talk about people's habits clearly. For example, you can say \"most people use smartphones,\" or \"some workers prefer paper notebooks.\" Saying \"all of my friends like digital books\" describes a specific group easily.\n\nIn the end, both digital and print media have great advantages. Digital files are best for fast daily communication. Paper is best for important books, legal documents, and quiet reading. Using both tools together gives us the best results.",
